<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narses</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 478–573</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narses was an Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> who rose to high office at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> and became one of his leading generals. He helped suppress the Nika riots in 532 and, in command of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a> from 551, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/totila">Totila</a> at Taginae and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teia">Teia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> Lactarius. He then destroyed a Frankish and Alemannic invasion at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casilinum">Casilinum</a> in 554 and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> until about 567.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narses.jpg" alt="Narses" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vahan.hovh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narses.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
